{"name":"Macaroni and Cheese","hex":"#ffb97b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"macaroni and cheese","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of macaroni cheese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/macaroni_and_cheese"}],"entries":[{"title":"Macaroni and cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Macaroni and cheese is a pasta dish of macaroni covered in cheese sauce, most commonly cheddar sauce. Its origins trace back to cheese and pasta casseroles in medieval England. The traditional macaroni and cheese is put in a casserole dish and baked in the oven; however, it may be prepared in a saucepan on top of the stove, sometimes using a packaged mix such as became popular in the mid-20th century. The cheese is often included as a Mornay sauce added to the pasta. It has been described as \"comfort food\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg/330px-Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaroni_and_cheese","wikidata":"Q378341"},{"title":"Macaroni","blocks":[{"text":"Macaroni, known in Italian as maccheroni, is a pasta shaped like narrow tubes. Made with durum wheat, macaroni is commonly cut in short lengths; curved macaroni may be referred to as \"elbow macaroni\". Some home machines can make macaroni shapes but, like most pasta, macaroni is usually made commercially by large-scale extrusion. The common curved shape is created by different speeds of extrusion on opposite sides of the pasta tube as it comes out of the machine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Macaroni2.jpg/330px-Macaroni2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaroni","wikidata":"Q20019"},{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese","wikidata":"Q10943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg/500px-8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg/500px-8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baked macaroni and cheese","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A8.28.12CheeseburgerMacByLuigiNovi1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Cicis-Mac%26Cheese-Pizza.jpg/500px-Cicis-Mac%26Cheese-Pizza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Cicis-Mac%26Cheese-Pizza.jpg/1280px-Cicis-Mac%26Cheese-Pizza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Cicis-Mac%26Cheese-Pizza.jpg/500px-Cicis-Mac%26Cheese-Pizza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Macaroni and cheese pizza","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACicis-M